<%#- STRUCTURAL fork, and the sharpest of the three. Both styled variants mark
     the current page with a CLASS (btn-active, or a background utility). With
     no stylesheet there is nothing to carry that signal, so the current page
     has to change ELEMENT — <strong> rather than a styled <span> — and the
     inert prev/next markers become plain text. A class-token map cannot
     express a change of tag name.

     Emitted ONCE per app into app/views/shared/, so nothing here may name the
     resource: everything resource-shaped (the wrapper id, the anchor target,
     the page-number window) arrives as a local from the list partial. The
     `--css=` marker below is how a later scaffold run detects a variant
     mismatch — keep it. -%>
<%%# locals: (page: 1, page_count: 1, pages: [], anchor:, id:) -%>
<%%# Shared page control (--css=<%= css_variant %>), rendered above and below
    every scaffolded list. The links are anchors to the list, so a click also
    does the browser's own fragment jump; data-turbo="false" keeps Turbo Drive
    out. `on` returns a { data: } hash — merge, don't splat, or the anchor
    stops scrolling. %>
<%% page_data = ->(n) { { turbo: false }.merge(on(:go_to_page, with: { page: n })[:data]) } %>
<%%# The wrapper always renders, so idiomorph always has a node to pair with. %>
<div id="<%%= id %>">
  <%% if page_count > 1 %>
    <nav aria-label="Pagination">
      <%%# Prev/next go inert at the ends rather than disappearing, so the
          control keeps its position across a page change. %>
      <%% if page == 1 %>
        <span aria-disabled="true">«</span>
      <%% else %>
        <%%= link_to "«", anchor, rel: "prev",
                    "aria-label": "Previous page", data: page_data.(page - 1) %>
      <%% end %>

      <%% pages.each do |n| %>
        <%% if n.nil? %>
          <span aria-hidden="true">…</span>
        <%% elsif n == page %>
          <strong aria-current="page"><%%= n %></strong>
        <%% else %>
          <%%= link_to n, anchor, "aria-label": "Page #{n}", data: page_data.(n) %>
        <%% end %>
      <%% end %>

      <%% if page == page_count %>
        <span aria-disabled="true">»</span>
      <%% else %>
        <%%= link_to "»", anchor, rel: "next",
                    "aria-label": "Next page", data: page_data.(page + 1) %>
      <%% end %>
    </nav>
  <%% end %>
</div>
